            "review_title": "Review at Issun Boushi(一寸法師2)Japan Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Anika\nDa Nang, Vietnam8 contributions\n0\nWarm Welcome, Fresh Flavors – My Favorite Sushi Spot in Da Nang!\nApr 2025 • Solo\nI stopped by Issue Bishi today for an early lunch around 11:00 AM—turns out I was the first customer of the day. The staff gave me a warm welcome and even opened the door, which made a lovely first impression.\n\nI was quite hungry and ordered from their 120K VND lunch menu: fatty sashimi salmon belly (absolutely delicious), a tuna maki, and a nigiri set with tender cooked white fish. Everything tasted incredibly fresh and high-quality.\n\nWhile waiting, I saw the team hand-making dumplings on the spot. I usually hesitate with dumplings, but I’m so glad I tried them—the pork dumplings were crispy outside, gooey and hot inside. A total win!\n\nThey also served complimentary green tea, a comforting miso soup, and a small steamed veggie appetizer. These little extras really made the experience special.\n\nYes, the prices are slightly higher than other sushi places in Da Nang, but the quality more than justifies it. This was my third sushi restaurant in town, and Issue Bishi is now my favorite.\n\nThe only small detail: the sushi rice was a bit warm. But honestly, that just confirmed how fresh everything was. I think they weren’t expecting someone so early and did their best to serve everything fresh and fast—which I appreciated.\n\nIf you value freshness, friendly service, and authentic Japanese flavors, this place is worth every dong. Highly recommended!\nRead more\nWritten April 10, 2025",
