            "review_text": "journey960\nAustralia67 contributions\n0\nVietnamese restaurant with Japanese food.\nOct 2019 • Solo\nOne can not fault the food but something that has never been achieved is high standard of service Japan is known for.\nThere is no feeling of welcome in the restaurant and if one has travelled in Japan you do not need to have Kaiseki course or have Maiko next to you.Service in Japan is way of life and since the food ticks the box if the tardiness of the servers can be improved would be a great experience.\nI disslike imitations but attention to the customer is not there.Train the staff not only the chef.\nThere is a feeling if you want to come and stay come if not do not.\nI had several times missed the appetiser/service which is common courtesy in Japan.\nGrilled items vary often the density of grill less cooked or overcooked.I am talking about same items.\nConsistency is missing.Manners.Then you can say you have been to a Japanese restaurant instead of saying I had Japanese food.\nIt is a down to earth restaurant with non appealing decor as many said come to eat.\nConsidering the price\nRead more\nWritten October 27, 2019",
