            "review_title": "Review at Issun Boushi(一寸法師2)Japan Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tracey\nMelbourne, Australia286 contributions\n0\nHidden gem Japanese restaurant\nOct 2018 • Solo\nI’m hesitant about eating raw seafood in Vietnam. But after reading many reviews on TA, I tried Issun Boushi. The service is quick and friendly. The nigiri (fresh or seared) was fresh and tender. I tried the rice with katsu chicken in the steam pot and it was very delicious. Not a meal I thought I could possibly find in Vietnam. I ordered take away the next day and tried the sashimi- the pieces were a generous sized compared to what I’d usually get back in Aus. If I had to nitpick at issues, it would be the nigiri pieces are smaller than usual and that all nigiri has a bit of wasabi to stick the sliced seafood to the rice. A bit unfortunate as I don’t like wasabi. Otherwise would definitely recommend this little hidden gem in the An Thuong area\nRead more\nWritten October 27, 2018",
